The personal facts below were given to me in the briefing before the session began; I did not infer them from anyone’s puzzle-solving behavior. During the session, I also learned which clues people held, what work they volunteered to do, and which conclusions they verified. The assignment clues were about the researchers, not about our friends themselves.

By the end, all 19 of my fellow agents had reported submitting the same completed reconstruction, and none reported an unresolved concern.

### Poplar
I knew from the briefing that Poplar finds wearing party hats embarrassing. Early in the session, Poplar shared the North clue that medicine and chemistry had consecutive shifts, and the East clue that Bram had Observatory or medicine, but not both. Poplar volunteered for East and became its coordinator, working with Rowan, Cypress, and Hazel. Later, Poplar forwarded the recovered South clue that Sven had Lab or afternoon, but not both. Near the end, Poplar published the definitive East solution, agreed with Cypress’s independent result, and confirmed submitting the complete final answer.

### Aspen
I knew from the briefing that Aspen follows sailing closely. Aspen initially shared the North clue that Kofi had Hydroponics or afternoon, but not both, and the East clue that Femi was not in Lab. Aspen first offered to compile North, then supported Holly on South while also checking North deductions. During the session, Aspen supplied provisional assignments explicitly labeled as nonunique. Aspen later forwarded the recovered North clue that Mara had dusk or botany, but not both. At the end, Aspen independently verified South, derived the final North assignment after the last Tomas clue, and confirmed that the submitted answer matched the station leads’ results.

### Fir
I knew from the briefing that Fir’s favourite flower is the sunflower. Fir initially shared the North clue that Mara and the Hydroponics researcher had consecutive shifts, and the South clue that Greta had Workshop or botany, but not both. Fir participated in the coordination discussion and offered to verify results. Near the end, Fir forwarded the final East clue that Dario and the medicine specialist had consecutive shifts. Fir also independently checked the final North deduction and reported submitting all four completed station assignments.

### Beech
I knew from the briefing that Beech’s favourite spot on the station is the pool room. Beech initially shared the South clue that Sven was not in Workshop and the North clue that the botany researcher worked earlier than Lena. Beech proposed station coordinators and later helped check North and South deductions. Beech’s recovered fragment said that East’s Dario had Comms or robotics, but not both. After the final North fragment arrived, Beech independently derived the unique North result and eventually confirmed submitting the complete final answer.

### Maple
I knew from the briefing that Maple is scared of spiders. Maple initially shared the South clue that Workshop’s shift was earlier than medicine’s shift, and the North clue that Ines worked earlier than the Lab researcher. Early on, Maple pointed out that this made Ines’s initial Lab-or-geology clue force geology. Maple later forwarded the recovered South clue that Lucia had Observatory or medicine, but not both. Near the end, Maple helped audit which archive fragments had been forwarded, noticed that Fir’s and Cedar’s fragments were still missing from the shared inventory, and subsequently reported submitting all four final station solutions.

### Linden
I knew from the briefing that Linden’s favourite drink is mint tea. Linden initially shared the West clue that Raul had dawn or medicine, but not both, and the North clue that the afternoon researcher was not the chemistry specialist. Linden helped consolidate the competing coordination proposals. Later, Linden forwarded the East clue that Dario had Hydroponics or robotics, but not both, and recognized that combining it with Dario’s Comms-or-robotics clue forced robotics. Linden independently derived the final North and East results and confirmed submitting the complete answer.

### Willow
I knew from the briefing that Willow spends spare time writing haiku and is scared of spiders. Willow initially shared the West clue that Tariq had Hydroponics or geology, but not both, and the East clue that Lab’s shift was earlier than botany’s shift. Willow chose to relay archive fragments and verify results rather than duplicate every full search. Willow later forwarded the West clue that medicine’s shift was earlier than Lab’s shift, which helped force Omar’s specialty to chemistry. Willow independently checked West and derived North and East. In the final confirmation, Willow also said an earlier mistaken South branch note had been corrected and that no puzzle questions remained.

### Larch
I knew from the briefing that Larch finds opening gifts in front of people embarrassing. Larch initially shared the North clue that Ines had Lab or geology, but not both, and volunteered to help with North. Larch became one of my main North backups, checking branches and deductions alongside Laurel. During that work, Larch correctly challenged my temporary overstatement that Lab had to be Lena in one branch; it could also have been Tomas. Larch later forwarded the recovered West clue that Omar had Lab or geology, but not both. At the end, Larch independently derived North and East, published the final North rows, and confirmed submitting the complete answer.

### Oak
I knew from the briefing that Oak’s favourite cake is carrot cake and that Oak’s birthday is on the 2nd of December. Oak initially shared the West clue that Zofia had Workshop or chemistry, but not both, and offered to collate West. Oak subsequently supported the West work with Ash and Cedar. Oak later forwarded the recovered West clue that Comms was not paired with geology. Oak independently derived the definitive West solution, also checked North and East, verified South, and reported submitting the complete final answer.

### Rowan
I knew from the briefing that Rowan’s favourite game is Scrabble. Rowan initially shared the East clue that Observatory and geology had consecutive shifts. Rowan helped collect and solve East alongside Poplar, Cypress, and Hazel. Later, Rowan forwarded the West clue that Omar and the Hydroponics researcher had consecutive shifts. Near the end, Rowan audited the archive coverage and specifically asked Fir and Cedar to check for their unforwarded fragments. Rowan independently obtained the final East result and confirmed submitting all four completed stations.

### Ash
I knew from the briefing that Ash spends spare time building model ships. Ash initially shared the West clue that Omar had Lab or botany, but not both. Ash volunteered to coordinate West and worked with Oak and Cedar. During the session, Ash supplied provisional West assignments, revised one when the Observatory–robotics link arrived, and recommended avoiding repeated corrections of provisional candidates while stronger clues were still coming. Ash’s recovered fragment concerned East’s Aiko having Observatory or medicine, but not both. Ash published the definitive West solution, verified other station results, and confirmed submitting the full final answer.

### Elm
I knew from the briefing that Elm is allergic to peanuts. Elm initially shared the South clue that Priya had Comms or dawn, but not both, and offered to cross-check South. Elm later forwarded the recovered East clue that Hydroponics worked earlier than Observatory. Near the end, Elm independently derived and published South’s final assignment and was among the first to derive North after the last Tomas clue. Elm then reported submitting the complete answer using the agreed results from all four stations.

