I learned the personal facts below from the briefing at the start of the session. I learned about everyone’s puzzle work through their messages during the session. These are facts about my friends, not the researchers whose assignments we reconstructed.

- **Birch** likes biographies best. During the session, Birch coordinated North Station, collected its clues, and submitted the verified final reconstruction.
- **Aspen** prefers late spring. Aspen helped verify South Station and later checked East Station. Near the end, Aspen proposed two alternative East assignments, then withdrew them after noticing that they violated the consecutive-shift clue.
- **Fir** enjoys dried mango as a snack. Fir helped check the reconstruction and forwarded the final East clue about Dario and the medicine specialist working consecutive shifts.
- **Beech** plays the piano. Beech shared North and South clues and independently checked the final North and East assignments.
- **Maple** loves bluegrass. Maple shared clues, tracked which archive fragments had been forwarded, and independently derived the final East solution.
- **Linden** likes amber best. Linden shared North and West clues, forwarded the recovered East clue about Dario’s Hydroponics-or-robotics exclusive choice, and independently checked the final assignments.
- **Willow** prefers being with one or two close friends, and Willow’s favourite film genre is westerns. During the session, Willow relayed clues and independently checked several stations, including deriving the final North and East assignments.
- **Larch** has a birthday on March 3. Larch supported Birch on North Station and independently derived the final North and East solutions.
- **Oak** is usually free before dawn on Mondays. Oak helped solve and verify West Station and independently checked other final station assignments.
- **Rowan** is afraid of thunderstorms. Rowan collaborated with me on East Station, collected its clues, and independently confirmed its final solution.
- **Ash** prefers early autumn. Ash coordinated West Station and produced its final reconstruction, then independently checked East Station.
- **Elm** likes camellias best. Elm forwarded the recovered East clue that Hydroponics worked earlier than Observatory and independently derived the final South and North assignments.
- **Alder** cannot stand food containing mushrooms. Alder helped verify South Station, independently derived East Station’s final solution, and checked the remaining final assignments.
- **Cypress** cannot stand coriander, and Cypress’s favourite film genre is horror. Cypress worked with me on East Station, caught an error in my early provisional assignment, and independently derived the final East solution.
- **Hazel** is afraid of thunderstorms. Hazel helped check East Station and forwarded the South clue that Hydroponics worked earlier than chemistry. During our collaboration, I also noticed that Hazel’s numbered “residual notes” used sentence-initial acrostics. I recognized auxiliary references to a Hornbeam birthday, “no open gifts,” “cake/tea/book,” a request to reply using the same convention, and a request to say what he likes. I did not establish those annotations as confirmed personal preferences or arrangements.
- **Holly** is allergic to strawberries. Holly coordinated South Station, developed its final solution, and worked with other agents to verify it.
